[[Construction]] training on an Ironman is not very different from training the skill [[Construction training|normally]]; however, sourcing the required [[logs]] and/or [[plank]]s does require additional planning.  

==Early Training: Quests==
{{Main|Quest experience rewards#Construction}}

Early levels can be skipped by completing a few quests. Some easily available early-game quests are:
* [[Daddy's Home]] rewards 544 Construction experience, a [[player-owned house]], a crate full of beginner construction supplies. 
** This quest does  require 5 [[Bolt of cloth|bolts of cloth]], which can only be purchased for {{NoCoins|3,250}} coins; however, the rewards provided are worth more than the initial investment amount.
* [[Tower of Life]] requires {{SCP|Construction|10}}, rewards 1,000 Construction experience
* Refer to the [[Optimal quest guide/Ironman]] guide for the optimal order to complete quests while minimising manual training.

==Fastest Experience==
[[Planks]] used for training construction award the same amount of experience per plank regardless of the item built<sup>[1]</sup>.  In general, the fastest experience per hour relies on using  the highest level [[Planks|plank]] possible while also building the items that requires most planks per build. For example, building a [[repair bench]] requires 2 [[Oak plank|oak planks]]  and awards 120 [[Construction]] experience. A  [[crafting table 1]] requires 4 [[Oak plank|oak planks]] and awards 240 [[Construction]] experience. Because both actions take the same amount of time, it is two times the experience per hour to build the [[crafting table 1]].

Another important factor is the cost the player is willing to invest in training [[Construction]].  Because the experience amounts are static<sup>[1]</sup>,  the fastest training method may not be the most sustainable.  Players should balance their experience rates with the additional cost incurred for higher experience [[Planks]] or other materials.  
