===Levels 16+: Oak planks===

* {{SCP|Construction|16}} - Make [[Crafting table 1|crafting table 1s]] in your [[Workshop]].
* {{SCP|Construction|33}} - Make [[Oak larder|oak larders]] in your [[kitchen]].

=== Levels 38+: Teak planks ===

* {{SCP|Construction|38}} - Make [[Teak table|teak tables]] in your [[dining room]].
* {{SCP|Construction|66}} - Make [[Teak garden bench|teak garden bench]] in  your [[Superior garden]].

=== Levels 40+: Mahogany planks ===

* {{SCP|Construction|40}} - Make [[Mahogany bookcase|mahogany bookcases]] in your [[parlour]], [[quest hall]], or [[study]].
* {{SCP|Construction|52}} - Make [[Mahogany table|mahogany tables]] in your [[Dining room]].

==Other methods==
===Passive training: Wintertodt===
Early levels can be bypassed by defeating [[Wintertodt]] while training [[Firemaking]]. Having a [[player-owned house]] is required to receive Construction experience from repairing braziers (4{{X}} player's Construction level). To maximize experience, train [[Construction]] to level 20 before doing Wintertodt. [[Wintertodt/Strategies#Solo_Method|Soloing Wintertodt]] will yield substantially more construction experience and loot rolls per hour at the cost of some Firemaking experience per hour.

=== Passive training: Tempoross ===
While slower than [[Wintertodt]], fixing the [[Totem pole|damaged totem poles]] during the [[Tempoross]] fight will award 4x the player's Construction level. To maximize experience, train [[Construction]] to level 20 before doing Tempoross.

