Completing Mahogany Homes contracts is an alternative training method that is more interactive and offers more experience per plank but much slower than traditional training methods. Mounted mythical capes with [[teak plank]]s offer up to three times higher experience per hour than adept Mahogany Homes contracts; this time save makes up for requiring more logs and coins if you can make approximately {{NoCoins|600,000}} coins per hour or if money is not the limiting factor.
<!--Adept (teak) contracts for Mahogany Homes are 140,000 experience per hour ish, but cost about 500ish teak planks per hour, while myth capes are 3 times that but cost 3300 planks per hour. So if you spend 3 hours doing contracts, that is the same experience for only 1500 planks. Teak planks are most optimistically worth 660 coins each, 500 to make planks and 160 coins from Managing Miscellania set to collect teaks (50,000 for 301 logs with 10 workers). Cutting them yourself is less efficient, so this is the best case. The 2 hours you save cost you close to 1,200,000 coins, plus some extra time making logs. Obviously if you do a lot of Slayer tasks, you eventually have enough cash, but for low and mid game accounts who want all the nice PoH features money still matters. In those cases, doing adapt contracts is generally better because they are so much more money efficient. -->

