This method requires you to teleport around Gielinor and rebuild the furniture of the citizens inhabiting various cities. There are 12 houses spread over [[Varrock]], [[Falador]], [[East Ardougne]] and [[Hosidius]]. All cities contain 3 possible houses to refurnish, and a house requires on average 13 planks to complete. Some furniture requires a steel bar. If you have a [[diary cape]], it is slightly faster to teleport with the diary cape to Sarah (Toby) and Ross (Two-pints). It is recommended to put your player-owned house in Hosidius since Barbara is close to the house portal. Charged [[ring of wealth|rings of wealth]] are recommended, as the teleport to Falador Park is a bit faster than the spellbook teleport. If you have a limited amount of ring of wealth charges, it is instead recommended to use [[Falador Teleport]]. Fill your rune pouch with teleports to Varrock, Home, and Ardougne, and have a charged [[Xeric's talisman|Xeric's Talisman]] equipped for Hosidius [[Mahogany Homes#Construction contracts|contracts]]. Ideally, you should only use the [[Falador east bank]] when you have a contract in Falador, and the bank in Hosidius when you have a contract at one of the two north houses (you use teleport to house for the south house). If you run out of supplies before reaching one of these banks, bank at [[Seers' Village|Seers Village]]. You should buy the [[plank sack]] as soon as possible, and then get the outfit pieces.

This method is significantly faster on the [[Lunar Spellbook|Lunar spellbook]], as players can obtain a new construction contract through the NPC Contact spell. For this method, fill your [[rune pouch]] with [[astral rune|astral]], [[cosmic rune|cosmic]], and [[air rune]]s (or equip a [[staff of air]]) and equip a charged Xeric's talisman and a ring of wealth. Players will also need to have teleport tablets for Varrock and Ardougne (and Falador, if not using a ring of wealth).

For players without a diary cape, it is marginally faster to equip a charged [[chronicle]] and teleport to the [[Champion's Guild]] when assigned a contract in Sarah's house along Varrock's southern wall.
===Levels 47-99: Mounted mythical capes===
At 47 Construction, [[Mythical cape (mounted)|mounted mythical capes]] become available with the completion of [[Dragon Slayer II]], which significantly reduces the amount of [[teak plank]]s needed for training. Constructing mounted mythical capes increases the experience per plank to 123 rather than 90 because of a bonus 100 experience for using the [[mythical cape]].

Items cannot be dropped in building mode and it is possible to receive a full inventory of planks from the butler before removing the mounted mythical cape. It cannot be removed without inventory space for the cape, so a [[plank sack]] or equipable item in your inventory can be used to make space temporarily.

==Obtaining Supplies==
Early construction supplies can be gathered manually; however, there are a few helpful methods when starting out:  

* Picking up [[Plank|regular planks]] that spawn near the [[Barbarian Outpost]] and in [[Port Khazard]] are recommended as both locations are near to a [[bank]]. 
* Defeating [[Tempoross]] and collecting its [[Reward pool|rewards]] can provide [[Plank|regular]] and [[Oak plank|oak planks]] along with a lot of other Ironman-friendly supplies. 
* Early [[shipwreck salvaging]] provides [[Plank|regular]] and [[Oak plank|oak planks]]; however, the salvaging locations may be far from a bank.  
** Salvaging  also provides [[Sawmill coupon|sawmill coupons]] which  can be exchanged for free planks at a [[Sawmill]]. 
* Mobsters from [[Intelligence Gathering]]  often drop planks when killed.

Additional supplies can also be gathered by completing  the following: 

* [[Teak logs|Teak]] or [[mahogany logs]] can also be passively obtained via [[Managing Miscellania]] every day. 
** If collecting [[maple logs]] for [[Fletching]], put 5 workers on teak or mahogany Woodcutting. Mahogany is faster but more expensive and teak is only recommended if attempting to save some money on Construction training.
* Wintertodt [[Reward Cart|rewards]] can provide a decent supply of various logs as well depending on the player's Woodcutting level.
* High-level players can also get Construction supplies from combat activities such as the [[Chambers of Xeric]], [[Zulrah]], and [[Callisto]].
* The most consistent way of obtaining planks of any type is by cutting the logs and then having a player-owned house [[butler]] convert them into planks and bank them for you. 
** For the fastest possible gathering and experience rates is by using [[Tick_manipulation#1.5-tick_Woodcutting|1.5-tick woodcutting]] when gathering player-grown teak or mahogany logs on [[Fossil Island]]. 
** If training Woodcutting simultaneously, make sure you get the most [[anima-infused bark]] to buy [[sawmill voucher]]s as you can redeem one sawmill voucher to get one extra plank for free, depending on the type of log in the inventory.
* With the introduction of [[Auburnvale]], it is now the closest sawmill to a bank, beating out the  [[Woodcutting  Guild]] for those that would prefer the standard method.

